      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0126",
      "sequence": 138,
      "meaning": "When Kāma entered that hermitage, he used his illusion to create spring: many-coloured trees flowered, cuckoos called, bees hummed, and a delightful threefold breeze fanned the fire of desire. Rambhā and other young celestial women, accomplished in every art of Love, sang in rippling melodies and sported in many ways. Encouraged, Kāma tried every device, yet none of his arts touched the sage; frightened for himself, the defeated god of love clasped Nārada’s feet and spoke in deep distress. Who can cross the boundary of one whose mighty guardian is Lakṣmī’s Lord?",
