    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0127",
      "sequence": 139,
      "meaning": "Nārada felt no anger and consoled Kāma with kindly words. With permission, Kāma bowed and returned with his companions, telling Indra’s court of the sage’s gracious conduct; all marvelled, praised Nārada, and bowed to Hari. Nārada then went to Śiva, inwardly proud that he had conquered desire, and recounted the episode. Śiva affectionately urged him never to tell Hari this story, even if the subject arose, but that wholesome counsel did not please Nārada. Bharadvāja should hear the wonder: Hari’s will is powerful.",
