    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0128",
      "sequence": 140,
      "meaning": "Only what Rāma wills comes to pass; no one can make it otherwise. Displeased by Śiva’s advice, Nārada went first to Brahmā’s realm and later, singing Hari’s virtues with his fine vīṇā, reached the Milk Ocean where Lakṣmī’s Lord dwells. The Lord rose joyfully, seated the sage beside himself, and smilingly said that Nārada had shown grace after many days. Ignoring Śiva’s warning, Nārada told the whole tale of conquering Kāma. Raghupati’s māyā is so strong that no born being escapes delusion. With a grave face but gentle words, the Lord said that remembrance of Nārada dispels delusion, desire, vanity and pride.",
