      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0129",
      "sequence": 141,
      "meaning": "The Lord tells Nārada that delusion arises only in a mind without knowledge and dispassion, and asks how Love could trouble one wise and devoted to the vow of celibacy. Nārada proudly credits everything to the Lord’s grace. The compassionate Lord sees that a great tree of pride has sprouted in his heart and resolves, for his servant’s good, to uproot it quickly. Nārada bows and leaves with swelling ego; Śrīpati then sets his formidable māyā in motion, creating on the road a city a hundred yojanas wide and more splendid in every way than his own abode.",
