    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0130",
      "sequence": 142,
      "meaning": "The enchanted city is inhabited by men and women so beautiful that they seem like embodied Loves and Ratis. Its king, Śīlanidhi, possesses countless horses, elephants and troops, the splendour of a hundred Indras, and every excellence of beauty, glory, strength and policy. His daughter Viśvamohinī, the very all-virtuous māyā of Hari, is beautiful enough to enchant Lakṣmī herself. Countless kings assemble for her self-choice ceremony. Curious Nārada enters the city, learns what is happening, and goes to the palace, where the king honours and seats him, shows him the princess, and asks him to discern all her merits and faults.",
